 "text": "Jasper County, IN - Treasurer\nMonday - Friday\n8am - 4pm C.S.T.\n219-866-4930\n115 W Washington St\nRensselaer, IN 47978\nfab fa-facebook-square\nHours, Location, & Contact\nMonday - Friday\n8am - 4pm C.S.T.\n219-866-4930\n115 W Washington St\nRensselaer, IN 47978\nfab fa-facebook-square\nHome\nGovernment County Code\nCounty Commissioners\nCounty Council\nDirectory\nEmployment\nFinancial Documents\nDepartments Airport\nAssessor\nAuditor\nCoroner\nCounty Clerk\nEmergency Management\nHealth Department\nHighway Department\nHuman Resources\nJasper Co. Fair Association\nPlanning & Development\nPurdue Extension Office\nRecorder\nSheriff's Department\nSoil & Water Conservation\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nVeterans Services\nBoards Animal Control\nBoard of Zoning Appeals\nDrainage Board\nEconomic Development\nPlan Commission\nTourism\nWeed Control Board\nJustice System & Courts CASA\nChild Support\nCommunity Corrections\nCounty Clerk\nJasper Co. Circuit Court\nJasper County Justice Reinvestment Advisory Council\nJasper County Sheriff’s Office\nJasper Co. Superior Court\nProbation\nProsecuting Attorney\nResidents Electronic Sign Request\nLocal Links\nOnline Payments\nPermits & Procedures\nServices Index\nTownship Trustees\nVoting and Elections\nSearch\nDepartment\nTREASURER\nContact Us\nHours: Mon-Fri: 8am-4pm\nExcluding Holidays\nPhone: (219) 866-4938\nContacts\nTammy McEwan\nTreasurer\n115 W Washington St\nSuite 201\nRensselaer, IN 47978\nGet Directions\nPayment Options Property Tax Deductions Property Tax Sale Tax Sale Tax Statement Inquiries\nNo item found!\nThe office of the County Treasurer is a constitutional office. The constitution of Indiana and Indiana statutory law provides for the election of a treasurer in each county. The treasurer is responsible for the collection of county property taxes and is the custodian for all money belonging to the county.\nThe treasurer is also responsible to invest the public funds in a manner which provides the highest investment return with maximum security.\nThe Treasurer is responsible for the mailing of the tax statements and for the collection and distribution of the taxes generated in Jasper County. The treasurer also collects drainage assessments, excise tax, sewer liens, inn keepers tax and inheritance tax.\nTerm: 4 years - elected - two term limit in 12 years.\nChief function of the Treasurer is to collect and retain custody of and disperse county funds.\nMails and collects property taxes\nAlso collects Inheritance taxes, excise taxes, inn keepers taxes.\nFurnishes clearances for:\nAlcoholic beverage licenses\nMobile home moving permit or transfer of ownership\nKeep record of property owner's addresses\nInvest funds.\nFlat Menu | Accessibility | Website Terms | GIS Data & Property Record Cards | Facebook Page\nWe are an equal opportunity employer. All applicants will be considered for employment without attention to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, identity, national origin, veteran or disability status.\nPowered by SDL\n© Copyright. All Rights Reserved.\nSearch\nHome\nGovernment County Code\nCounty Commissioners\nCounty Council\nDirectory\nEmployment\nFinancial Documents\nDepartments Airport\nAssessor\nAuditor\nCoroner\nCounty Clerk\nEmergency Management\nHealth Department\nHighway Department\nHuman Resources\nJasper Co. Fair Association\nPlanning & Development\nPurdue Extension Office\nRecorder\nSheriff's Department\nSoil & Water Conservation\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nVeterans Services\nBoards Animal Control\nBoard of Zoning Appeals\nDrainage Board\nEconomic Development\nPlan Commission\nTourism\nWeed Control Board\nJustice System & Courts CASA\nChild Support\nCommunity Corrections\nCounty Clerk\nJasper Co. Circuit Court\nJasper County Justice Reinvestment Advisory Council\nJasper County Sheriff’s Office\nJasper Co. Superior Court\nProbation\nProsecuting Attorney\nResidents Electronic Sign Request\nLocal Links\nOnline Payments\nPermits & Procedures\nServices 